{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>Then Moshe set apart.</b> After he struck Sihon and Og. And the commandment has already been explained in the chapter of Masei, and here he mentions the act, to recall this kindness along with the other kindnesses he did for them. And concerning himself Moshe says thus, and it is as though it were written אז הבדלתי — like 'when a man offers from you an offering to HaShem' (i.e., in the first person), 'this is the matter that HaShem commanded you' (i.e., in the first person), and so many others."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:57.388712956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}